    - Lighthouse final scores
  Update docs/performance.md, docs/accessibility.md with final numbers.
  Update README.md to reflect the completed project.
  Then — and only then — declare the project complete.

## DEFINITION OF DONE

The project is complete when ALL of these are true:

  - Milestones 0, A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K all passed their gates.
  - Lighthouse Performance ≥ 85 on production build (mobile-throttled).
  - Lighthouse Accessibility = 100.
  - Lighthouse Best Practices ≥ 95.
  - Lighthouse SEO = 100.
  - Reduced-motion path verified on every section.
  - WebGL fallback verified.
  - 5-minute scroll soak: heap stable.
  - Zero console errors and zero console warnings from project code.
  - All 12 sections render real content.
  - Configurator updates 3D in real time.
  - Exploded view separates and reassembles correctly.
  - README reflects the actual state of the project.

## FINAL INSTRUCTION

Begin with Milestone E closure. Proceed through the sequence without
pausing between milestones. Paste raw gate output for every milestone.
If a gate fails, fix and re-run. Continue until Milestone K is complete
and the Definition of Done is fully satisfied.

If you reach a point where you genuinely cannot proceed, report the
blocker in one sentence and stop. Otherwise, keep going.

Do not ask "should I proceed?" — the answer is yes. The user has
authorized the full sequence.